   166	    // userId is what lets the client profile show that person's OWN page history
   167	    // and their location (portal visits especially). Anonymous marketing traffic
   168	    // resolves to null and is unaffected. Wrapped so an auth hiccup never blocks
   169	    // best-effort capture.
   170	    //
   171	    // EXCEPT while an admin is impersonating: `currentUser()` resolves to the
   172	    // TARGET customer (that's the whole point of impersonation), but `ip`
   173	    // above is the ADMIN's own real, physical address -- the browser making
   174	    // this request never moves. Attaching the target's id would write THIS
   175	    // request under the customer's own identity with the admin's IP/location,
   176	    // which is exactly what corrupted admin/users/[id]'s "Location"/"Sign-in
